      "description": "Oberlin College & Conservatory Applicant Portal | Search Jobs Skip to Main Content Jobs at Oberlin Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Contact Us Benefits Student Employment Search  Postings (35) Hide Search Options To view open positions, please enter your search criteria below.  You may view all open positions by not specifying any search criteria and clicking the Search button. Keywords Posted Within Any time period Last Day Last Week Last Month Position Type No Selection Faculty Professional Staff Support Staff Student Workers Temporary Workers Department No Selection Academic Departments and Programs Academic Services Admissions Allen Memorial Art Museum Assoc. V/P of Finance Athletics Programs Campus Safety Center for Information Technology College General Administration College On/Off Campus Programs College Project Accounts College of Arts and Sciences Communications Office Community & Government Departments Community Services Conference Services Conservatory Admissions Office Conservatory Departments & Program Conservatory General Administration Conservatory On/Off Campus Programs Conservatory Project Accounts Conservatory Summer Programs Dean of Students Facility Operations Facility Ops/Dorm Building Maintenance Facility Planning/Construction Financial Aid Human Resources Department Investment Library Music Theater Office of Advancement Office of Institutional Research Office of Off Campus Studies Office of Registrar Office of Student Union Office of the President President Project Accounts R&DH Admin Residential Services Secretary of College Shansi Departments Student Health & Wellness Services Student Life and Services Student Organizations V/P for Finance Go to search results page: Previous 1 2 Next (35) To view the position details and/or apply to an open position, click on the position title or the View Details link.  If you would like to bookmark a position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. Posting Number Department Postion Type Job Close Date OCL Digital Collaborative -  Library Student Assistant STU152590PS Library Operations Student Workers 09/07/2026 The OCL Digital Collaborative is looking for two reliable and responsible students to produce highly accurate OCR (Optical Character Recognition) results for our newspaper digitization project. You will work with one of the industry’s best OCR programs, Abbyy FineReader PDF, to create editable and searchable text from scanned images. You must love to read and appreciate the quirky layout of old... View Details Bookmark Research Help Desk Library Student Assistant - Fall 2026 STU152589PS Research & Instruction Student Workers 09/14/2026 This position is responsible for excellent customer service by providing research and library help through online chat and in person at the Research Help and Circulation desks. The job offers a great opportunity to become more familiar with the library and gain research and public service skills. View Details Bookmark Football Filmer STU152587PS Men's Football Student Workers Assist the football team by filming at practice and games. View Details Bookmark Office of the Dean of Students - Student Assistant STU152586PS Dean of Students' Office Student Workers The student assistant will support the daily operations in the Dean of Students Office and report to the Executive Assistant to the VP/Dean of Students and Office Manager by assisting with administrative, technological and operational tasks. This position provides an excellent opportunity to gain hands-on experience in operational processes within a higher education environment.The assistant wi... View Details Bookmark Networking Assistant STU152584PS Enterprise Infrastructure Student Workers A great opportunity for a detail-oriented student interested in computer networking. We work ‘behind the scenes’ on campus to keep the wired and wireless networks humming! The successful applicant(s) will be scheduled to work during business hours (M-F, between 8AM and 4:30PM). There may be occasional weekend or evening hours. There is an opportunity to work full-time (40 hrs/week) during the s... View Details Bookmark Peer Career Advisor – Career Support and Outreach STU152582PS Career Services Student Workers The Peer Career Advisor (PCA) serves as a student leader within Career Exploration & Development (CED), providing peer-to-peer career support while assisting with employer engagement, career programming, campus outreach, and post-graduation outcomes initiatives. Working closely with Career Advisors, PCAs help students navigate career resources, prepare for internships and employment, and in... View Details Bookmark Audiovisual Equipment Assistant Fall 2026 STU152572PS Academic Technolgy Student Workers 10/01/2026 Assist patrons with equipment rental needs and usage for class projects andorganizational events. Prepare and return equipment orders. Trackinventory accessories on items such as camera kits, lighting kits and audio kits.At times, you may be required to deliver, set-up, and operate AV equipment for campususe. This includes projectors, screens, document cameras, sound systems, TV carts, etc.You ... View Details Bookmark Digital Portfolio Office Assistant STU152571PS College Winter Term Student Workers 08/14/2026 The Center for Engaged Liberal Arts (CELA) seeks a part-time student assistant to support the Digital Portfolio Office and Oberlin’s use of the Digication ePortfolio platform. This position combines technical support, student engagement, assessment, and administrative project work. Student assistants help faculty, staff, and students use digital portfolios to document academic, co-curricular, a... View Details Bookmark BA+BFA Admissions Ambassador - Overnight Host Fall 2026 STU152574PS Admissions Office Student Workers 09/04/2026 The Office of Admissions is hiring BA+BFA Admissions Ambassadors to host Prospective BA+BFA students overnight in PRAX house! BA+BFA Ambassadors are required to host prospective students in their dorms during overnight programs the nights of Tuesday September 22 and Tuesday October 27.There may also be opportunities to appear on panels, help visitors find their way across campus, and connect wi... View Details Bookmark Susan Duncan ’75 and Leo Fisher ’75 Curatorial Fellow in Modern and Contemporary Art STU152579PS Art Museum Operations Student Workers 08/22/2026 This fall, the Allen Memorial Art Museum is launching three year-long curatorial fellowships, supported by the Susan Duncan ’75 and Leo Fisher ’75 AMAM Curatorial Fellowship Fund. One fellowship is available in each of the museum’s three curatorial collections (Asian Art, European and American art, and Modern and Contemporary Art). The fellows will engage in curatorial research as well as provi... View Details Bookmark Susan Duncan ’75 and Leo Fisher ’75 AMAM Curatorial Fellowship in Asian Art STU152577PS Art Museum Operations Student Workers 08/21/2026 This fall, the Allen Memorial Art Museum is launching three year-long curatorial fellowships, supported by the Susan Duncan ’75 and Leo Fisher ’75 AMAM Curatorial Fellowship Fund. One fellowship is available in each of the museum’s three curatorial collections (Asian art, European and American art, and Modern and Contemporary Art). The fellows will engage in curatorial research as well as provi... View Details Bookmark Con Audio Student Recording Engineer STU152573PS Audio Services Department Student Workers 09/30/2026 Student Recording Engineers’ duties include recording student, guest, and faculty recitals, running sound reinforcement for jazz recitals, assisting with large recording sessions, and operating cameras for live streaming of concerts.Must be responsible, motivated, punctual, and attentive to detail. Must be able to lift 50 lbs.Number of hours varies based on concert/event schedule. Hours are lig... View Details Bookmark Reproducible Media Print Lab Monitor STU152569PS Art Studio Student Workers The department of Studio Art is currently seeking reproducible media print lab monitors for the fall 2026 semester. View Details Bookmark Photo Lab Monitor (Student Worker) STU152570PS Art Studio Student Workers The Studio Art Program is seeking Photo Lab Monitors. View Details Bookmark Media Associate STU152563PS Art Studio Student Workers The Studio Art Media Lab Associate position is available for students who have a familiarity with or interest in working with digital and analog technologies. Students with skills in video, audio, photography, printing, interactive media, projection mapping, micro-controllers, coding and other areas are all welcome to apply. The successful candidate will be available 6 (min)-12 (max) hours a we... View Details Bookmark Ninde College Access Support Specialist -Student Worker STU152416PS Bonner Center for Service & Learning Student Workers 02/12/2027 Description:The Ninde College Access Program serves the Oberlin City School District. The program serves all students at Oberlin High School, providing college access services including college tours, college application support, ACT/SAT testing sign up, financial aid application support, scholarship application distribution and filing, and other supports for students regarding the college and ... View Details Bookmark Education Programs Tutor-Student Worker STU152145PS Bonner Center for Service & Learning Student Workers 03/02/2027 Education Programs tutors work with children in grades Kindergarten through fifth grade (literacy) and ninth grade (math), within Oberlin City School District classrooms and community after school programs in Lorain County. Tutors work with children on literacy and/or mathematical concepts and includes tutoring and enrichment programming. Tutors may work with children in small groups or one-on-... View Details Bookmark Ninde Scholar Tutor STU150214PS Bonner Ctr for Service & Learning Student Workers 02/19/2027 The Ninde College Access Program serves 7th–12th grade students in the Oberlin City School District. The program works with students who have a high financial need, and/or may be the first in their families to attend college. The role of the tutor is to provide academic support in classes that may challenge students, discuss college going and college preparation, reinforce student success, ment... View Details Bookmark Wellness Ambassador STU152325PS Health Promotion Student Workers Wellness Ambassadors serve as a resource through the Office of Health Promotion and Prevention Services and will play a crucial role in supporting fellow students by providing education, resources, and support related to mental health, wellness, and academic success. The Wellness Ambassadors will directly report to the Director of Health Promotion and Prevention Services. View Details Bookmark Fabrication Lab Student Worker STU152556PS Art Studio Student Workers The student worker will assist the Fabrication Lab Technician in the lab during weekly fabrication lab hours. The student worker will work up to 5 – 8 hrs per week, in person, starting in August 2026. The student worker will be hired for the duration of the semester, with the potential for a renewed contract at the end of the semester.Fabrication Lab student workers are responsible for assistin... View Details Bookmark Impact Investment Fellow - Student Worker STU152426PS CELA Student Workers 08/31/2025 Interested in the evolving field of impact finance? Want to engage with administrators to make a difference on campus and beyond? Hoping to gain skills that will impact your own career development? If this sounds like you, apply to be an Impact Investment Fellow and help advise Oberlin’s endowment in balancing financial and social returns! View Details Bookmark Impact Investment Fellow STU152555PS CELA Student Workers 08/31/2026 Do you believe students have a lot to contribute to the ongoing discourse regarding the climate crisis and social justice?Are you passionate about building research projects from scratch and growing ideas into disruptive change?Are you looking to engage with administrators and make a difference on campus and beyond?Are you hoping to gain skills that will impact your own career development?Do yo... View Details Bookmark Community Based Work Study Student Position STU152549PS Bonner Center for Service & Learning Student Workers 02/19/2027 Description: The Oberlin Community Based Work Study Program hires Oberlin College students with a Federal Work Study Award to work within community organizations in Oberlin. Each year Oberlin College hires students to work at over 16 community partners, serving the Oberlin community through work at non-profit organizations that serve a variety of needs like food insecurity, the arts, historical... View Details Bookmark Stockroom Assistant, Chemistry & Biochemistry STU152542PS Chemistry & Biochemistry Student Workers 09/08/2026 The Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry invites applications for Stockroom Assistants for the Fall of 2026. Majoring or planning to major in chemistry or biochemistry is preferred but not required.Chemistry & Biochemistry Stockroom Assistants will get the opportunity to develop their understanding of the materials at hand, gain further knowledge of topics that they previously learned... View Details Bookmark CHEM 254 Teaching Assistant, Chemistry & Biochemistry STU152541PS Chemistry & Biochemistry Student Workers 09/08/2026 The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry invites applications for Teaching Assistants (TAs) for Fall 2026. There are openings for assisting CHEM 254 lab sections. Applicants must be pursuing an interest in the sciences in order to be considered (pursuing a major in chemistry or biochemistry is preferred, but not required).Chemistry & Biochemistry TAs will get the opportunity to develop ... View Details Bookmark CHEM 211 Teaching Assistant, Chemistry & Biochemistry STU152540PS Chemistry & Biochemistry Student Workers 09/08/2026 The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry invites applications for Teaching Assistants (TAs) for the Fall 2026 semester. There are openings for assisting CHEM 211 lab sections. Applicants must be pursuing an interest in the sciences in order to be considered (pursuing a major in chemistry or biochemistry is preferred, but not required).Chemistry & Biochemistry TAs will get the opportunit... View Details Bookmark CHEM 205 Teaching Assistant, Chemistry & Biochemistry STU152539PS Chemistry & Biochemistry Student Workers 09/08/2026 The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry invites applications for Teaching Assistants (TAs) for the Fall 2026 semester. There are openings for assisting CHEM 205 lab sections. Applicants must be pursuing an interest in the sciences in order to be considered (pursuing a major in chemistry or biochemistry is preferred, but not required).Chemistry & Biochemistry TAs will get the opportunit... View Details Bookmark CHEM 102 Teaching Assistant, Chemistry & Biochemistry STU152538PS Chemistry & Biochemistry Student Workers 09/08/2026 The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry invites applications for Teaching Assistants (TAs) for the Fall 2026 semester. There are openings for assisting CHEM 102 lab sections. Applicants must be pursuing an interest in the sciences in order to be considered (pursuing a major in chemistry or biochemistry is preferred, but not required).Chemistry & Biochemistry TAs will get the opportunit... View Details Bookmark CHEM 101 Teaching Assistant, Chemistry & Biochemistry STU152537PS Chemistry & Biochemistry Student Workers 09/08/2026 The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry invites applications for Teaching Assistants (TAs) for the Fall 2026 semester. There are openings for assisting CHEM 101 lab sections. Applicants must be pursuing an interest in the sciences in order to be considered (pursuing a major in chemistry or biochemistry is preferred, but not required).Chemistry & Biochemistry TAs will get the opportunit... View Details Bookmark Living Machine Operator STU152533PS Environmental Studies Student Workers The Environmental Studies Program will be hiring two (2) Living Machine Operators, one (1) of whom must be able to work DURING THE SUMMER OF 2026. We are seeking applicants with experience in lab sciences, demonstrated ability to work independently, and a strong work ethic. The student operators will share the responsibilities of caring for the Living Machine, as well as the building and ground... View Details Bookmark Go to search results page: Previous 1 2 Next Office of Human Resources Oberlin College 173 West Lorain Street Oberlin OH 44074 http://new.oberlin.edu/office/human-resources/ Phone: (440) 775-8430 Fax: (440) 775-8683 Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. human.resources@oberlin.edu 2015 © Oberlin College | Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
